1
00:00:03,002 --> 00:00:04,839
OKAY, THIS IS IT.

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,423
YOU SURE YOU WANT
TO DO THIS?

3
00:00:06,465 --> 00:00:08,133
( laughing )

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,721
HELLO, MRS. ROSS!

5
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:16,141
WHY, HELLO, MR. RACHEL!

6
00:00:22,773 --> 00:00:24,483
WHOA!

7
00:00:24,525 --> 00:00:25,567
OH, MY GOD.

8
00:00:25,609 --> 00:00:27,110
( rapid footsteps )

9
00:00:27,152 --> 00:00:28,863
HURRY! HURRY! HURRY UP!

10
00:00:28,904 --> 00:00:30,155
YEAH, YEAH, OKAY.

11
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:31,198
HURRY! HURRY!

12
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,117
OH, MY GOD!

13
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:36,036
IS EVERYBODY GETTING MARRIED?!

14
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:40,749
NO RUNNING IN THE CHAPEL.

15
00:00:40,791 --> 00:00:42,877
HEY, DON'T YOU GIVE ME
ANY OF YOUR...

16
00:00:42,918 --> 00:00:43,878
HEY!

17
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,212
HEY.

18
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:46,964
HEY, WHAT ARE
YOU GUYS DOING HERE?

19
00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:48,465
ROSS AND RACHEL
LEFT US A MESSAGE

20
00:00:48,507 --> 00:00:49,967
SAYING THEY WERE
GETTING MARRIED.

21
00:00:50,009 --> 00:00:51,510
ISN'T THAT WHY
YOU GUYS ARE HERE?

22
00:00:51,552 --> 00:00:52,511
YES. WELL, YES...

23
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:55,263
WHY ELSE WOULD
WE BE HERE?

24
00:00:56,932 --> 00:00:58,433
WELL, WHAT HAPPENED?

25
00:00:58,475 --> 00:00:59,601
DID WE MISS IT?

26
00:00:59,643 --> 00:01:01,311
WE ACTUALLY MISSED IT.

27
00:01:01,353 --> 00:01:03,438
WELL, MAYBE YOU WOULDN'T HAVE

28
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,482
IF YOU COULD RUN
IN THE CHAPEL!

29
00:01:05,524 --> 00:01:06,942
THIS IS INSANE.

30
00:01:06,984 --> 00:01:08,402
WHAT'S THE BIG DEAL?

31
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:10,195
YOU KNOW, IT'S NOT LIKE
IT'S A REAL MARRIAGE.

32
00:01:10,237 --> 00:01:11,697
WHAT?

33
00:01:13,032 --> 00:01:17,036
IF YOU GET MARRIED IN VEGAS,
YOU'RE ONLY MARRIED IN VEGAS.

34
00:01:18,203 --> 00:01:19,580
Monica:
WHAT ARE YOU
TALKING ABOUT?

35
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:21,248
IF YOU GET MARRIED
IN VEGAS, YOU'RE
MARRIED EVERYWHERE.

36
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:23,333
REALLY?

37
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:25,044
YEAH.

38
00:01:25,084 --> 00:01:27,421
OH, MY GOD.

39
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:28,839
EH, WELL.

40
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:41,142
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

41
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:43,353
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

42
00:01:43,395 --> 00:01:45,606
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

43
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:50,611
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

44
00:01:50,652 --> 00:01:53,864
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

45
00:01:53,906 --> 00:01:56,199
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

46
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:59,411
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

47
00:01:59,453 --> 00:02:02,497
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

48
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,178
( clattering )

49
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:19,014
HMM...

50
00:02:21,683 --> 00:02:23,769
OH.

51
00:02:29,858 --> 00:02:32,778
( groans )

52
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:34,738
( gasps )

53
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,991
( both screaming )

54
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:48,127
WHY ARE WE IN
BED TOGETHER?

55
00:02:48,167 --> 00:02:49,920
I DON'T KNOW.

56
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:52,547
DO YOU...
DO YOU HAVE

57
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:53,882
ANY CLOTHES ON?

58
00:02:53,924 --> 00:02:55,759
YES.

59
00:02:55,801 --> 00:02:56,551
REALLY?

60
00:02:56,593 --> 00:02:57,176
NO.

61
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:02,557
BUT WE DIDN'T HAVE...

62
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:06,770
SEX, DID WE?

63
00:03:06,812 --> 00:03:08,605
I DON'T...

64
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:12,818
I DON'T REMEMBER MUCH
ABOUT LAST NIGHT.

65
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:14,778
IT WAS SUCH A BLUR.

66
00:03:14,820 --> 00:03:15,863
OH!

67
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:17,781
I REMEMBER LAUGHING.

68
00:03:17,823 --> 00:03:19,282
I LAUGHED A LOT.

69
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:20,951
THEN WE DIDN'T
HAVE SEX.

70
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:25,664
( groans )

71
00:03:25,706 --> 00:03:29,168
OH, I MEAN, WE WERE
REALLY DRUNK.

72
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:31,628
I'M GLAD WE DIDN'T
DO ANYTHING STUPID.

73
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:33,254
TELL ME ABOUT IT.

74
00:03:37,551 --> 00:03:38,844
MORNING, PHEEBS.

75
00:03:38,886 --> 00:03:40,179
HEY.

76
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:43,932
WELL, MY MOVIE HAS BEEN
OFFICIALLY CANCELED.

77
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:45,600
JOEY, I'M SO SORRY.

78
00:03:45,642 --> 00:03:48,227
YOU WANT SOME
OF MY BREAKFAST?

79
00:03:48,269 --> 00:03:50,313
NAH. I'M TOO
DEPRESSED TO EAT.

80
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:53,483
I'LL PROBABLY BE EATING
IN, LIKE, FIVE MINUTES.

81
00:03:53,525 --> 00:03:55,986
SO I GUESS I'LL JUST
FLY HOME WITH YOU GUYS.

82
00:03:56,028 --> 00:03:57,445
WHAT TIME'S YOUR FLIGHT?

83
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:58,405
WHAT ABOUT MY CAB?

84
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:00,239
I DON'T NEED THAT ANYMORE.

85
00:04:00,281 --> 00:04:02,242
NO, JOEY, YOU
BORROWED MY CAB.

86
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:04,036
YOU HAVE TO DRIVE IT BACK.

87
00:04:04,078 --> 00:04:06,788
I DON'T WANT TO DRIVE
ALL THE WAY BACK BY MYSELF.

88
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:07,998
I GET SO LONELY.

89
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:10,042
OH, OH, HOW ABOUT
IF YOU COME WITH ME?

90
00:04:10,084 --> 00:04:12,586
I DON'T KNOW, IT'S
SUCH A LONG TRIP.

91
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:13,670
IT'LL BE GREAT.

92
00:04:13,712 --> 00:04:15,756
WE CAN TALK
AND PLAY GAMES, HUH?

93
00:04:15,797 --> 00:04:19,426
THIS COULD BE OUR CHANCE
TO, LIKE, RENEW OUR FRIENDSHIP.

94
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:23,138
ARE YOU ASKING
ME TO HAVE A
FRIEND-AISSANCE?

95
00:04:24,181 --> 00:04:25,974
SURE?

96
00:04:26,016 --> 00:04:27,392
ALL RIGHT.

97
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:29,811
ALTHOUGH I DON'T THINK
WE REALLY NEED ONE, BABY.

98
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:31,354
I NEVER STOPPED LOVIN' YOU.

99
00:04:32,564 --> 00:04:33,648
HEY.

100
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:35,109
Joey:
HEY.

101
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:37,527
SO HAS ANYBODY TALKED
TO DR. AND MRS. GELLER YET?

102
00:04:37,569 --> 00:04:38,820
MM-HMM. YEAH.

103
00:04:38,862 --> 00:04:40,072
THEY LEFT ME A MESSAGE.

104
00:04:40,114 --> 00:04:41,281
THEY SHOULD BE HERE
ANY MINUTE.

105
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,741
WHERE IS THE WAITRESS?

106
00:04:42,783 --> 00:04:44,451
I'M STARVING.

107
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:48,205
IT'S A BUFFET, MAN.

108
00:04:48,247 --> 00:04:51,541
OH, HERE'S WHERE I WIN
ALL MY MONEY BACK.

109
00:04:54,211 --> 00:04:56,171
LISTEN, I GOT
TO TALK TO YOU.

110
00:04:56,213 --> 00:04:58,215
SURE. WHAT'S UP?

111
00:05:05,764 --> 00:05:08,850
MONICA AND I ALMOST
GOT MARRIED LAST NIGHT.

112
00:05:08,892 --> 00:05:10,102
OH, MY GOD!

113
00:05:10,144 --> 00:05:11,519
THAT'S HUGE!

114
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:13,855
HEY!

115
00:05:13,897 --> 00:05:15,065
WAIT A MINUTE.

116
00:05:15,107 --> 00:05:16,900
WHY WASN'T I INVITED?

117
00:05:16,942 --> 00:05:18,193
AND WHO WAS
GOING TO BE

118
00:05:18,235 --> 00:05:19,402
YOUR BEST MAN?

119
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:20,737
DON'T SAY ROSS.

120
00:05:20,779 --> 00:05:22,156
DO NOT SAY ROSS.

121
00:05:22,197 --> 00:05:24,574
LOOK, I JUST DON'T THINK
THAT MONICA AND I

122
00:05:24,616 --> 00:05:26,785
ARE READY TO GET MARRIED
YET, YOU KNOW?

123
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:29,204
I MEAN, I LOVE HER
AND EVERYTHING, BUT...

124
00:05:29,246 --> 00:05:31,999
SEEING ROSS AND RACHEL
COMING OUT OF THAT CHAPEL

125
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,875
WAS LIKE A... LIKE
A WAKE-UP CALL

126
00:05:33,917 --> 00:05:36,628
THAT MONICA AND I ARE
MOVING SO FAST, YOU KNOW.

127
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:38,922
HOW DO I TELL HER
WITHOUT CRUSHING HER?

128
00:05:38,964 --> 00:05:41,133
OH.

129
00:05:41,175 --> 00:05:43,510
TELL HER SHE'S NOT
MARRIAGE MATERIAL.

130
00:05:46,096 --> 00:05:47,931
WHAT?

131
00:05:47,973 --> 00:05:50,475
GIRLS SAY IT TO ME
ALL THE TIME.

132
00:05:50,517 --> 00:05:52,435
AND BELIEVE ME

133
00:05:52,477 --> 00:05:53,812
IF SHE'S ANYTHING
LIKE ME

134
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:55,647
SHE'S JUST GOING
TO BE RELIEVED.

135
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,901
HOW DO I TELL CHANDLER
THAT IT'S TOO SOON?

136
00:05:59,943 --> 00:06:01,278
IT'S GOING
TO BREAK HIS HEART.

137
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,238
HE'S GOING TO THINK
I DON'T LOVE HIM ANYMORE.

138
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,239
WELL, YOU DON'T.

139
00:06:04,281 --> 00:06:05,740
YES, I DO.

140
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:07,909
WELL, GOOD, GOOD.
I WAS JUST TESTING YOU.

141
00:06:07,951 --> 00:06:09,870
Chandler:
HI.

142
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,579
OH, HI, HI.

143
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:14,624
YOU KNOW, WE WERE JUST
TALKING ABOUT BACON.

144
00:06:14,666 --> 00:06:16,751
NO, WE WERE TALKING
ABOUT TENNIS.

145
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:18,545
TENNIS IS MORE BELIEVABLE.

146
00:06:20,714 --> 00:06:22,174
HEY.

147
00:06:22,216 --> 00:06:23,550
HEY.
HEY.

148
00:06:23,591 --> 00:06:24,885
HI.

149
00:06:24,926 --> 00:06:26,970
THANK YOU.

150
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,849
MM.

151
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:37,731
WHAT?

152
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:38,982
ARE WE GOING
TO TALK ABOUT

153
00:06:39,024 --> 00:06:40,942
WHAT YOU GUYS
DID LAST NIGHT, OR...?

154
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:42,694
WHAT... WHAT DO YOU
MEAN LAST NIGHT?

155
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:43,528
NOTHING-NOTHING...

156
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,239
NOTHING HAPPENED
LAST NIGHT.

157
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,489
YEAH.

158
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:47,824
UH-HUH.

159
00:06:47,866 --> 00:06:49,993
ROSS INVITED US
ALL TO WATCH.

160
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:53,538
RACH, WE WEREN'T
GOING TO MISS

161
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,249
OUR FRIENDS
GETTING MARRIED.

162
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:57,709
( gasps ):
WHO GOT MARRIED?!

163
00:06:59,169 --> 00:07:00,962
YOU DID?

164
00:07:01,004 --> 00:07:02,881
WHAT?
WHAT?

165
00:07:02,923 --> 00:07:04,132
WE... WE... HELLO?

166
00:07:04,174 --> 00:07:06,093
NO, WE DIDN'T.
WE DIDN'T GET MARRIED.

167
00:07:06,134 --> 00:07:07,135
THAT'S RIDICULOUS.

168
00:07:07,177 --> 00:07:09,179
( both gasp )

169
00:07:12,473 --> 00:07:13,641
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.

170
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:15,143
I REMEMBER BEING
IN A CHAPEL.

171
00:07:15,185 --> 00:07:17,979
THEY WOULD NOT LET
US GET MARRIED

172
00:07:18,021 --> 00:07:19,147
WHEN WE WERE
THAT DRUNK.

173
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:21,482
THEY LET YOU GET MARRIED
WHEN YOU'RE DRUNK.

174
00:07:21,524 --> 00:07:23,860
MOST PEOPLE GETTING MARRIED
IN VEGAS ARE DRUNK.

175
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,821
I'M DRUNK
RIGHT NOW.

176
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:31,826
WHAT, I CAN'T HAVE
A MIMOSA WITH BREAKFAST?

177
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:33,120
I'M ON
VACATION.

178
00:07:33,161 --> 00:07:34,662
WHAT ARE YOU GUYS
GOING TO DO?

179
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:37,249
I GUESS WE JUST FIND
A DIVORCE LAWYER?

180
00:07:37,291 --> 00:07:38,792
WELL, I THINK...

181
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,585
I THINK ROSS
ALREADY HAS ONE.

182
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:44,464
THIS ONE'S FREE, RIGHT?

183
00:07:44,505 --> 00:07:45,966
BECAUSE YOU PAID
FOR THE FIRST TWO

184
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:47,634
SO YOU GET THE THIRD ONE
FOR FREE.

185
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:49,052
LAUGH IT UP.

186
00:07:49,094 --> 00:07:50,387
BUT THE JOKE'S
ON YOU.

187
00:07:50,429 --> 00:07:52,847
BECAUSE WE DON'T NEED
TO GET DIVORCED, OKAY?

188
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:54,975
WE'RE JUST GOING
TO GET AN ANNULMENT.

189
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:56,351
Joey:
AN ANNULMENT?

190
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:59,813
ROSS, I DON'T THINK
SURGERY'S THE ANSWER HERE.

191
00:08:01,815 --> 00:08:03,691
OH, THAT'S
YOUR THING.

192
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:05,402
WHAT?

193
00:08:05,444 --> 00:08:07,737
YOUR THING,
YOUR THING, YOU KNOW.

194
00:08:07,779 --> 00:08:10,115
YOU'RE THE GUY
WHO GETS DIVORCED.

195
00:08:10,157 --> 00:08:11,325
OH, YEAH.

196
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:12,700
IT MIGHT
BE TRUE.

197
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:14,453
IT'S NOT
MY "THING."

198
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:17,205
I DO NOT LOVE
GETTING DIVORCED.

199
00:08:17,247 --> 00:08:18,539
YES, YOU DO.

200
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:19,916
THIS IS YOUR
THIRD DIVORCE.

201
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:21,418
GOD, YOU LOVE
DIVORCE SO MUCH

202
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:23,211
YOU'RE PROBABLY
GOING TO MARRY IT

203
00:08:23,253 --> 00:08:24,587
AND THEN...

204
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:28,133
AND THEN IT WON'T WORK OUT

205
00:08:28,175 --> 00:08:31,094
SO YOU'RE GOING TO HAVE
TO DIVORCE IT, DIVORCING GUY.

206
00:08:31,136 --> 00:08:32,137
( laughing )

207
00:08:32,179 --> 00:08:33,472
I'M SO DRUNK.

208
00:08:41,271 --> 00:08:42,897
SO WHAT DO YOU THINK
WE SHOULD DO?

209
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:44,232
I DON'T KNOW.

210
00:08:44,274 --> 00:08:45,733
I-I-I KNOW I LOVE YOU.

211
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:47,444
I KNOW I LOVE YOU.

212
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:54,117
SO WHERE ARE WE
ON THE WHOLE

213
00:08:54,159 --> 00:08:57,412
GOING-BACK-TO-THE-PLACE-
WHERE-THEY-HAVE-ALL-
THE-MARRIAGES THING?

214
00:08:57,454 --> 00:08:58,746
I LOVE YOU.

215
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:01,416
THAT'S A GOOD QUESTION.

216
00:09:01,458 --> 00:09:03,293
WELL, LAST NIGHT WE
LET THE DICE DECIDE.

217
00:09:03,335 --> 00:09:05,295
MAYBE WE SHOULD LEAVE
IT UP TO FATE AGAIN.

218
00:09:05,337 --> 00:09:06,838
I LOVE YOU.

219
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:10,425
YES, WE DON'T GET MARRIED
UNLESS THERE'S A SIGN, OKAY?

220
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:12,802
SO, SAY... SAY YOU ROLL
ANOTHER EIGHT

221
00:09:12,844 --> 00:09:14,388
THEN THERE IS
A DEFINITE SIGN

222
00:09:14,429 --> 00:09:15,930
THAT WE SHOULD GET MARRIED.

223
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:17,598
ALL RIGHT, EIGHT,
WE GET MARRIED

224
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:20,601
BUT TWO, THREE, FOUR, FIVE,
SIX, SEVEN, NINE, 10, 11, 12

225
00:09:20,643 --> 00:09:21,769
WE DON'T GET MARRIED.

226
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:23,104
SOUNDS GREAT.
OKAY.

227
00:09:23,146 --> 00:09:24,314
OKAY, WE GOT
A SHOOTER.

228
00:09:24,356 --> 00:09:25,648
MONEY, PLEASE.

229
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:26,816
YOU READY?

230
00:09:26,858 --> 00:09:27,942
READY.

231
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,736
COME ON, EIGHT.

232
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:35,116
YES, YES, EIGHT.

233
00:09:36,617 --> 00:09:37,744
Man:
EIGHT, EASY EIGHT.

234
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:43,791
WOW, I CAN'T BELIEVE I
ACTUALLY ROLLED AN EIGHT.

235
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:46,127
THAT WAS SO UNLIKELY.

236
00:09:46,169 --> 00:09:48,796
WELL, LET'S GET MARRIED...

237
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:50,131
I GUESS.

238
00:09:50,173 --> 00:09:51,883
THAT WASN'T
A HARD EIGHT.

239
00:09:51,925 --> 00:09:53,510
LAST NIGHT I ROLLED
A HARD EIGHT.

240
00:09:53,552 --> 00:09:55,636
THAT'S RIGHT, IT WAS
THE WRONG KIND OF EIGHT.

241
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:56,637
NO WEDDING! DAMN IT!

242
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:58,306
( both groaning )

243
00:09:58,348 --> 00:09:59,349
I WANTED IT SO BAD.

244
00:10:02,769 --> 00:10:03,644
WANT TO GO PACK?

245
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:05,021
YEAH.

246
00:10:06,106 --> 00:10:08,442
WE'RE DOING THE
RIGHT THING, RIGHT?

247
00:10:08,483 --> 00:10:09,984
OF COURSE WE ARE.

248
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,361
WE LEFT IT UP
TO FATE.

249
00:10:11,403 --> 00:10:13,654
